          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जिताना — jitānā — \"to bring victory to; to win (a match) for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अरुण ने आख़िर में दौड़कर टीम को जिताया। Aruṇ ne ākhir meṁ dauṛkar ṭīm ko jitāyā. In the end Arun ran it in and won the match for the team."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने अपनी टीम को जिताया, usne apnī ṭīm ko jitāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जिताना (jitānā) is the causative of jītnā, \"to win\", which comes from Sanskrit jita, \"won, conquered\" (CDIAL 5224): to make someone win."
            }
          ]
        },
